OL,3,GNEWSADrought talks 'unite people to
OL,4,Aprotect nature'
OL,5,
OL,6,FDrought and extreme weather "brought
OL,7,Fcommunities together", a wildlife
OL,8,Fmanager has said.
OL,10,FRandy Mayers, an area reserve manager
OL,11,Ffor urban parks in Exeter for Devon
OL,12,FWildlife Trust, attended a meeting at
OL,13,FDowning Street on 21 September with
OL,14,Fpeople from homeless agencies, RNLI,
OL,15,Fambulance and fire services to discuss
OL,16,Fthe impacts of drought and extreme
OL,17,Fweather.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34302
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F343A1790659607
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSADrought talks 'unite people to
OL,4,Aprotect nature'
OL,5,
OL,6,FSummer 2026 was the UK's hottest on
OL,7,Frecord, according to provisional data
OL,8,Ffrom the Met Office, which Mayers said
OL,9,F"impacted quite significantly on the
OL,10,Flandscape".
OL,12,FHe said: "The fires and these
OL,13,Fextremities has really brought
OL,14,Fcommunities together and... this idea
OL,15,Fthat we really need to look after our
OL,16,Flandscape and our natural resources."
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
